"expression":"well-known","decision":"REJECT","reason":"「よく知られた」までで評価的な名声を含まないことが多く、このpromptとの対応はやや弱い。"},{"expression":"renowned","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「名高い・名声のある」を直接表す主要語で、文章語として独立した学習価値がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["famous","renowned"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"一般語famousと文章語renownedはいずれもpromptへの主要回答で、canonicalとは別に覚える価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01905","prompt_ja":"賞","canonical_snapshot":"award","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["award","prize"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"prize","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"競技・コンテスト等の「賞」を表す基本語で、awardとは使い分けもあり学習価値が高い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["prize"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"prizeは「賞」の主要な別語で、MISS扱いより登録が妥当。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01906","prompt_ja":"並外れた","canonical_snapshot":"extraordinary","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["extraordinary","exceptional","remarkable","outstanding"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"exceptional","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"普通の水準を大きく超える「並外れた」を表す高頻度の主要形容詞。"},{"expression":"remarkable","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"注目に値するほど「並外れた」という意味で、一般・文章語双方で有用。"},{"expression":"outstanding","decision":"REJECT","reason":"主に「優秀な」の評価を強く帯び、単なる並外れたより意味が狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["exceptional","remarkable"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"主要な一般語2語を採用し、優秀さに寄りすぎるoutstandingは外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01907","prompt_ja":"称賛","canonical_snapshot":"praise","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["praise","admiration","acclaim"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"admiration","decision":"REJECT","reason":"内的な感嘆・敬意を表しやすく、表明された「称賛」とは一致しない場合がある。"},{"expression":"acclaim","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"公的・広範な称賛を表す主要語で、media/academicでも有用。"}],"after_paraphrases":["acclaim"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"acclaimは範囲がやや公的だが「称賛」の明確な主要表現で独立価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01908","prompt_ja":"聴衆","canonical_snapshot":"audience","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["audience","listeners","crowd"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"listeners","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「聴衆」を文字どおり聞き手として表す自然な高頻度語。"},{"expression":"crowd","decision":"REJECT","reason":"単なる群衆でも成立し、聞いている集団という意味を保証しない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["listeners"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"listenersはpromptへの直接的な別回答で、crowdは関連語に留まる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01909","prompt_ja":"講義","canonical_snapshot":"lecture","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["lecture","class","lesson"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"class","decision":"REJECT","reason":"授業・クラス全体を指し、講義形式そのものとは限らない。"},{"expression":"lesson","decision":"REJECT","reason":"個別の授業・学習単位まで広く、講義より意味範囲がずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"prompt-onlyでもlectureが最も直接的で、他候補は授業一般へ広がりすぎる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01910","prompt_ja":"ごみ袋","canonical_snapshot":"garbage bag","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["garbage bag","trash bag","bin bag"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"trash bag","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"米国英語で極めて一般的な「ごみ袋」の主要variant。"},{"expression":"bin bag","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"英国英語で一般的な「ごみ袋」の主要variantで、地域差として学習価値がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["trash bag","bin bag"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"US/UKの主要variantはいずれも実用性が高く、別表現として登録価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01911","prompt_ja":"送迎バス","canonical_snapshot":"shuttle bus","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["shuttle bus","shuttle","courtesy bus"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"shuttle","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"文脈上バス等の定期往復送迎を指す高頻度な短縮表現として自然。"},{"expression":"courtesy bus","decision":"REJECT","reason":"無料送迎などサービス提供側の意味を帯び、送迎バス一般より狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["shuttle"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"shuttleは送迎交通を表す一般的な別表現だが、courtesy busは条件が限定的。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01912","prompt_ja":"私のものの3倍の大きさだ","canonical_snapshot":"three times as large as mine","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["three times as large as mine","three times as big as mine","three times the size of mine"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"three times as big as mine","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"同じ倍率比較をより日常的なbigで表す自然な高頻度表現。"},{"expression":"three times the size of mine","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"倍率をsize名詞構文で表す主要な別construction。"}],"after_paraphrases":["three times as big as mine","three times the size of mine"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"会話的なas big as構文とsize構文はいずれも自然で独立した回答価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01913","prompt_ja":"someoneと少し話す","canonical_snapshot":"have a word with someone","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["have a word with someone","have a chat with someone","talk to someone for a bit"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"have a chat with someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"短く気軽に話す意味の非常に自然な会話表現。"},{"expression":"talk to someone for a bit","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「少し話す」を直接表す高頻度の一般表現で、promptへの回答として自然。"}],"after_paraphrases":["have a chat with someone","talk to someone for a bit"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"短時間の会話を表す2つの主要表現を採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01914","prompt_ja":"somethingするとすぐに","canonical_snapshot":"on doing something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["on doing something","upon doing something","immediately after doing something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"upon doing something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"on doingよりformalだが「〜するとすぐに」を表す標準的なconstruction。"},{"expression":"immediately after doing something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"時間関係を明示する高頻度表現で、promptへの対応が明確。"}],"after_paraphrases":["upon doing something","immediately after doing something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"formalなupon構文と明示的なimmediately afterはいずれも実用的な別表現。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01915","prompt_ja":"時差ぼけ","canonical_snapshot":"jet lag","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["jet lag"],"candidate_review":[],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"jet lagが標準的な固定表現で、別に登録すべき主要表現はない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01916","prompt_ja":"残念ながら〜だと思う","canonical_snapshot":"I'm afraid","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["I'm afraid","unfortunately, I think","I regret to say"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"unfortunately, I think","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"残念な判断を前置きする自然な一般表現で、promptへ直接対応する。"},{"expression":"I regret to say","decision":"REJECT","reason":"主に告知・発言への遺憾を示すformal表現で、「〜だと思う」一般より用途が狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["unfortunately, I think"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"unfortunately, I thinkは自然な主要代替だが、I regret to sayは発話場面に限定される。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01917","prompt_ja":"someoneにsomethingするよう助言する","canonical_snapshot":"advise someone to do something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["advise someone to do something","recommend that someone do something","suggest that someone do something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"recommend that someone do something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"助言として行動を勧める主要constructionで、formalにも一般にも有用。"},{"expression":"suggest that someone do something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"行動案を助言・提案する高頻度constructionとしてpromptに成立する。"}],"after_paraphrases":["recommend that someone do something","suggest that someone do something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"recommend/suggestの主要constructionはいずれも助言表現として高い学習価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01918","prompt_ja":"someoneを説得してsomethingさせる","canonical_snapshot":"persuade someone to do something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["persuade someone to do something","convince someone to do something","talk someone into doing something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"convince someone to do something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"現代英語で非常に一般的な「説得して〜させる」の主要表現。"},{"expression":"talk someone into doing something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"会話で頻出する句動詞型の説得表現で、独立した学習価値が高い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["convince someone to do something","talk someone into doing something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"一般語convinceと句動詞constructionの双方が主要回答として有用。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01919","prompt_ja":"臓器移植","canonical_snapshot":"organ transplant","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["organ transplant","organ transplantation"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"organ transplantation","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"医療・学術文脈で一般的な名詞形で、organ transplantとはregister差がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["organ transplantation"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"technical/formalなorgan transplantationは読解価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01920","prompt_ja":"ジャンクフード","canonical_snapshot":"junk food","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["junk food"],"candidate_review":[],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"junk foodが固定した標準表現で、主要な別表現はない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01921","prompt_ja":"somethingを辞める","canonical_snapshot":"resign from something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["quit something","leave something","give up something","resign from something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"quit something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"仕事・活動・習慣などを「辞める」の非常に高頻度な一般語。"},{"expression":"leave something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"組織・仕事等を辞める意味で自然かつ高頻度な一般表現。"},{"expression":"give up something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"習慣・活動を断念する意味には合うが、仕事・所属を辞める一般表現としては範囲が偏る。"}],"after_paraphrases":["quit something","leave something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"promptが広いため、resignより一般的なquit/leaveをMISSにする方が教育的に不適切。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01922","prompt_ja":"義務教育","canonical_snapshot":"compulsory education","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["compulsory education","mandatory education","compulsory schooling"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"mandatory education","decision":"REJECT","reason":"意味は通るが定着した用語としてはcompulsory education/schoolingより不自然で、追加価値が低い。"},{"expression":"compulsory schooling","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"学校教育に焦点を置く主要な定型表現で、政策・教育文脈でも有用。"}],"after_paraphrases":["compulsory schooling"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"compulsory schoolingは標準的な別表現だが、mandatory educationは登録価値が弱い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01923","prompt_ja":"大きな目標を実現する","canonical_snapshot":"fulfill an ambition","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["achieve a major goal","accomplish a major goal","realize a major goal","fulfill an ambition"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"achieve a major goal","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"goalとの最も基本的なcollocationで、promptへの主要回答。"},{"expression":"accomplish a major goal","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"目標を成し遂げる意味で自然な高頻度表現。"},{"expression":"realize a major goal","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するがachieve/accomplishより一般性が低く、追加価値は限定的。"}],"after_paraphrases":["achieve a major goal","accomplish a major goal"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"goalと結びつく主要collocation2種を採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01924","prompt_ja":"実現する","canonical_snapshot":"come true","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["come true","become a reality","materialize","realize"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"become a reality","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"計画・夢などが「実現する」を表す自然な定型表現。"},{"expression":"materialize","decision":"REJECT","reason":"予定・期待が現実化する用法はあるが、一般学習語としては用途が狭い。"},{"expression":"realize","decision":"REJECT","reason":"通常は目的語を取る「〜を実現する」で、無標の自動詞的promptには形が合いにくい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["become a reality"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"come trueと並ぶ主要な実現表現としてbecome a realityのみ採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01925","prompt_ja":"お仕事は何ですか","canonical_snapshot":"what do you do?","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["what do you do?","what do you do for a living?","what's your job?","what kind of work do you do?"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"what do you do for a living?","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"職業を尋ねる最も代表的な会話表現の一つ。"},{"expression":"what's your job?","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"直接的で基本的な職業質問としてpromptに成立する。"},{"expression":"what kind of work do you do?","decision":"REJECT","reason":"自然だが上記2表現に比べ追加の独立学習価値が小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["what do you do for a living?","what's your job?"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"職業を尋ねる主要な会話表現2種を採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01926","prompt_ja":"専攻は何ですか","canonical_snapshot":"what's your major?","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["what's your major?","what are you majoring in?","what do you study?"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"what are you majoring in?","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"大学等の専攻を直接尋ねる非常に自然な会話表現。"},{"expression":"what do you study?","decision":"REJECT","reason":"学んでいる科目一般を尋ねられ、正式な専攻とは限らない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["what are you majoring in?"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"majoring in構文はpromptに正確で、what do you study?は範囲が広すぎる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01927","prompt_ja":"somethingに申し込む","canonical_snapshot":"apply for something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["apply for something","sign up for something","register for something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"sign up for something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"サービス・講座・活動などへの「申し込む」の高頻度な会話表現。"},{"expression":"register for something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"講座・イベント等への登録申込を表す主要表現。"}],"after_paraphrases":["sign up for something","register for something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"応募系applyに加え、参加・登録系の主要表現もpromptが許容する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01928","prompt_ja":"〜するとすぐに","canonical_snapshot":"as soon as","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["as soon as","the moment","immediately after"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"the moment","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"節を導いて「〜するとすぐに」を表す高頻度の定型construction。"},{"expression":"immediately after","decision":"REJECT","reason":"後続形が名詞/動名詞中心で、同じ接続構文としては形がずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["the moment"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"the momentは接続表現として高価値だが、immediately afterは構文形が異なるため外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01929","prompt_ja":"somethingを卒業する","canonical_snapshot":"graduate from something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["graduate from something","finish something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"finish something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"課程を終えることは表せても、卒業資格の取得を保証しない。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"graduate fromが卒業を正確に表す標準construction。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01930","prompt_ja":"somethingすると決心している","canonical_snapshot":"be determined to do something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["be determined to do something","have made up one's mind to do something","be resolved to do something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"have made up one's mind to do something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「〜すると決心している」を表す高頻度のidiomatic construction。"},{"expression":"be resolved to do something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"正確だがformalで頻度が低く、追加の学習価値は限定的。"}],"after_paraphrases":["have made up one's mind to do something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"make up one's mind構文は実用性が高く、formalなresolvedは外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01931","prompt_ja":"大人になる","canonical_snapshot":"grow up","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["grow up","become an adult"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"become an adult","decision":"REJECT","reason":"意味は成立するが、語の組合せどおりの説明的表現で独立語彙としての増分価値が小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"grow upが日常英語の主要表現で、説明的なbecome an adultを追加する必要はない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01932","prompt_ja":"自分の道を進む","canonical_snapshot":"go my own way","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["go one's own way","follow one's own path","make one's own way"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"go one's own way","decision":"REJECT","reason":"canonicalのmyをone'sへ置き換えただけで、surface variantに当たる。"},{"expression":"follow one's own path","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"比喩的に自分の選んだ道を進む自然な主要表現。"},{"expression":"make one's own way","decision":"REJECT","reason":"自力で進む・成功する含意が強く、単に自分の道を進むより意味がずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["follow one's own path"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"人称置換は除外し、独立したpath表現のみ採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01933","prompt_ja":"進展しない","canonical_snapshot":"get nowhere","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["get nowhere","make no progress","not get anywhere"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"make no progress","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「進展しない」を直接表す高頻度で明確な表現。"},{"expression":"not get anywhere","decision":"REJECT","reason":"canonicalとほぼ同じidiomの否定形で、増分学習価値が小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["make no progress"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"formalにも一般にも使えるmake no progressを独立表現として採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01934","prompt_ja":"つまり","canonical_snapshot":"I mean","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["I mean","in other words","that is","namely"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"in other words","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"言い換えを導く「つまり」の代表的な定型表現。"},{"expression":"that is","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"説明・再定義を導く高頻度表現で、文章語でも会話でも有用。"},{"expression":"namely","decision":"REJECT","reason":"具体的な列挙・特定を導く用途に偏り、無標の「つまり」より狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["in other words","that is"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"言い換え・説明を導く主要2表現を採用し、namelyは用途の狭さから外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01935","prompt_ja":"somethingの価値を信じる","canonical_snapshot":"believe in something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["believe in something","believe in the value of something","have faith in something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"believe in the value of something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"promptをほぼ逐語展開しただけで独立した表現価値が小さい。"},{"expression":"have faith in something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"価値より信頼・有効性を信じる意味が強く、対応がずれる場合がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"canonicalが最も自然で、他候補は説明的または信頼の意味へずれる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01936","prompt_ja":"賞を受ける","canonical_snapshot":"receive an award","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["receive an award","win an award","win a prize","be awarded a prize"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"win an award","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"賞を獲得する際の非常に高頻度なcollocation。"},{"expression":"win a prize","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"競技・懸賞等で「賞を受ける」の基本的な別表現。"},{"expression":"be awarded a prize","decision":"REJECT","reason":"自然だがaward/prizeを組み替えた受動構文で、上記2表現より増分価値が小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["win an award","win a prize"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"winとの主要collocation2種は実用性が高く、別回答として登録価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01937","prompt_ja":"順応するのが難しいと感じる","canonical_snapshot":"find it hard to adjust","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["find it difficult to adjust","have difficulty adjusting","struggle to adjust","find it hard to adjust"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"find it difficult to adjust","decision":"REJECT","reason":"hard→difficultの近いsurface substitutionで、独立学習価値が小さい。"},{"expression":"have difficulty adjusting","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"困難を表す名詞constructionとして自然で高頻度。"},{"expression":"struggle to adjust","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"順応に苦労する意味を簡潔に表す高頻度表現。"}],"after_paraphrases":["have difficulty adjusting","struggle to adjust"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"単純な形容詞置換は外し、別construction2種を採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01938","prompt_ja":"背景","canonical_snapshot":"background","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["background","context","backdrop"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"context","decision":"REJECT","reason":"事情・文脈を指す語で、人物経歴や視覚的背景を含むbackground全般とは一致しない。"},{"expression":"backdrop","decision":"REJECT","reason":"舞台・視覚的背景や比喩的状況に限定され、prompt一般より狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"backgroundが多義の「背景」を最も広くカバーし、他候補は一部のsenseに偏る。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01939","prompt_ja":"世界的な","canonical_snapshot":"worldwide","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["worldwide","global","international"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"global","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"世界規模の・世界的なを表す最重要の現代英語形容詞。"},{"expression":"international","decision":"REJECT","reason":"複数国にまたがる意味で、必ずしも世界規模を意味しない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["global"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"globalは直接的な主要別語で、internationalは範囲が狭い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01940","prompt_ja":"名声","canonical_snapshot":"fame","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["fame","renown","reputation","prestige"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"renown","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"肯定的な「名声」を直接表す主要な文章語。"},{"expression":"reputation","decision":"REJECT","reason":"良し悪しを含む「評判」一般で、肯定的名声より意味範囲が広い。"},{"expression":"prestige","decision":"REJECT","reason":"尊敬・威信に焦点があり、知名度としての名声とはずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["renown"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"renownは名声の直接的な主要別語で、reputation/prestigeは意味軸が異なる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01941","prompt_ja":"蓄積する","canonical_snapshot":"accumulate","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["accumulate","build up","amass","pile up"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"build up","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"量・経験・圧力などが徐々に蓄積する高頻度phrasal verb。"},{"expression":"amass","decision":"REJECT","reason":"富・情報などを大量に集める他動詞用法に偏り、一般の蓄積より狭い。"},{"expression":"pile up","decision":"REJECT","reason":"物や問題が山積するイメージが強く、一般の蓄積には偏りがある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["build up"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"最も一般的な別表現build upのみを採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01942","prompt_ja":"ものすごい","canonical_snapshot":"tremendous","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["tremendous","incredible","amazing","enormous"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"incredible","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"程度・印象の強さを表す非常に高頻度な「ものすごい」の口語表現。"},{"expression":"amazing","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"驚くほどすごいという意味で日常会話の学習価値が高い。"},{"expression":"enormous","decision":"REJECT","reason":"大きさ・量の巨大さに寄り、一般的な「ものすごい」より用途が狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["incredible","amazing"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"日常会話で高頻度な2語を採用し、size寄りのenormousは外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01943","prompt_ja":"戦後の","canonical_snapshot":"postwar","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["postwar","post-war","after the war"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"post-war","decision":"REJECT","reason":"canonicalとの綴り・ハイフン差だけでsurface variant。"},{"expression":"after the war","decision":"REJECT","reason":"意味は通るが形容詞表現ではなく、単なる説明句で増分価値が低い。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"postwarが標準形で、綴りvariantや説明句をparaphrase化しない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01944","prompt_ja":"時代","canonical_snapshot":"era","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["era","age","period"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"age","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"歴史・文化上の「時代」を表す高頻度な主要語。"},{"expression":"period","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"一定の時間区分としての「時代」を表す基本語で、学術文脈でも重要。"}],"after_paraphrases":["age","period"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"歴史的ageと一般的periodはいずれもpromptへの主要回答。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01945","prompt_ja":"報酬","canonical_snapshot":"reward","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["reward","compensation","pay","remuneration"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"compensation","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"仕事・サービスへの報酬を表すbusiness上重要な主要語。"},{"expression":"pay","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"労働への報酬を表す最も基本的な高頻度語。"},{"expression":"remuneration","decision":"REJECT","reason":"正確だが頻度が低いformal語で、既存2語に加える増分価値は小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["compensation","pay"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"business語compensationと基本語payはともに高い実用価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01946","prompt_ja":"利己的な","canonical_snapshot":"selfish","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["selfish","self-centered","egotistical"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"self-centered","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"自分本位な・利己的なを表す高頻度の主要形容詞。"},{"expression":"egotistical","decision":"REJECT","reason":"自己重要感・うぬぼれに焦点があり、利己性そのものとはずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["self-centered"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"self-centeredは主要別表現だが、egotisticalは自己評価の高さに意味が寄る。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01947","prompt_ja":"満足している","canonical_snapshot":"satisfied","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["satisfied","content","pleased"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"content","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"現状に満足している状態を表す主要形容詞で、register差も有用。"},{"expression":"pleased","decision":"REJECT","reason":"特定の出来事に喜んでいる意味が強く、状態としての満足一般とはずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["content"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"contentは継続的な満足状態を表す主要別語。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01948","prompt_ja":"借りがある","canonical_snapshot":"owe","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["owe","be indebted to someone","be in debt"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"be indebted to someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"金銭・恩義の双方で「someoneに借りがある」を表すformalな主要表現。"},{"expression":"be in debt","decision":"REJECT","reason":"金銭的債務に限定されやすく、恩義を含むprompt一般より狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["be indebted to someone"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"恩義も含められるbe indebted to someoneを採用し、金銭限定の表現は外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01949","prompt_ja":"全部で","canonical_snapshot":"altogether","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["altogether","in total","in all","all told"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"in total","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"数量を合計して「全部で」を表す最も一般的な表現の一つ。"},{"expression":"in all","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"総計を示す簡潔な高頻度表現。"},{"expression":"all told","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するがややidiomaticで頻度が低く、追加価値は限定的。"}],"after_paraphrases":["in total","in all"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"高頻度の総計表現2種を採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01950","prompt_ja":"かなりの","canonical_snapshot":"considerable","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["considerable","substantial","significant","sizable"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"substantial","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"量・程度がかなり大きいことを表す主要なacademic/business語。"},{"expression":"significant","decision":"REJECT","reason":"重要性・統計的有意性の意味も強く、単なる程度の「かなりの」とずれやすい。"},{"expression":"sizable","decision":"REJECT","reason":"主に大きさ・量に偏り、considerableほど一般的ではない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["substantial"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"substantialは「かなりの」の主要formal別語として価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01951","prompt_ja":"合計・総額","canonical_snapshot":"sum","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["sum","total","amount"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"total","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"合計・総額を表す最も一般的な名詞で、日常・business双方で高頻度。"},{"expression":"amount","decision":"REJECT","reason":"単なる量・金額で、合計済みであることを必ずしも示さない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["total"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"totalはpromptに直接対応する基本語で、MISS扱いは不適切。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01952","prompt_ja":"栄光","canonical_snapshot":"glory","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["glory","honor","splendor"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"honor","decision":"REJECT","reason":"栄誉・名誉に焦点があり、輝かしい栄光そのものとは意味がずれる。"},{"expression":"splendor","decision":"REJECT","reason":"壮麗さ・華麗さを表し、成功・名誉としての栄光とは異なる。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"gloryが「栄光」を最も直接表し、他候補は隣接概念。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01953","prompt_ja":"厳しい","canonical_snapshot":"harsh","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["harsh","strict","severe","tough","rigorous"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"strict","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"規則・人の「厳しい」を表す最重要の基本語。"},{"expression":"severe","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"状況・天候・罰などの「厳しい」を表す主要語。"},{"expression":"tough","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"課題・状況が厳しいことを表す高頻度な会話語。"},{"expression":"rigorous","decision":"REJECT","reason":"基準・訓練・方法が厳格という限定的なformal用法に寄る。"}],"after_paraphrases":["strict","severe","tough"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"promptが多義なため、主要な人/状況/会話の3表現はいずれも高価値。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01954","prompt_ja":"繁栄","canonical_snapshot":"prosperity","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["prosperity","affluence","flourishing"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"affluence","decision":"REJECT","reason":"富裕さに焦点があり、経済・社会の繁栄一般より狭い。"},{"expression":"flourishing","decision":"REJECT","reason":"形容詞/動名詞的で、名詞「繁栄」の自然な同等回答になりにくい。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"prosperityが名詞「繁栄」の標準語で、他候補は意味または品詞がずれる。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01955","prompt_ja":"続く","canonical_snapshot":"last","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["last","continue","go on","persist"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"continue","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「続く」の最も基本的で広い動詞の一つ。"},{"expression":"go on","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"出来事・状態が続くことを表す高頻度の会話phrasal expression。"},{"expression":"persist","decision":"REJECT","reason":"問題・状態がしつこく続く含意が強く、無標の「続く」より狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["continue","go on"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"基本語continueと会話表現go onを採用し、persistは持続性の含意が強いため外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01956","prompt_ja":"永遠に","canonical_snapshot":"forever","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["forever","eternally","for good"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"eternally","decision":"REJECT","reason":"直接的だが文語・宗教/文学寄りで、追加の実用価値は限定的。"},{"expression":"for good","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「永久に・もう元に戻らず」の意味で会話に頻出する有用なidiom。"}],"after_paraphrases":["for good"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"永続を表す高頻度idiom for goodは独立学習価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01957","prompt_ja":"適切な","canonical_snapshot":"proper","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["proper","appropriate","suitable","adequate"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"appropriate","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"場面・目的に「適切な」を表す最重要のformal/general語。"},{"expression":"suitable","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"用途・人に合っている意味の高頻度な主要語。"},{"expression":"adequate","decision":"REJECT","reason":"十分なという最低基準の意味が中心で、適切さとは一致しない。"}],"after_paraphrases":["appropriate","suitable"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"appropriate/suitableは用途の異なる主要別語で、adequateは意味軸が違う。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01958","prompt_ja":"資格","canonical_snapshot":"qualification","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["qualification","credentials","eligibility"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"credentials","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"職業・専門上の